      fullTextSummary: 'The dispute arose from an Islamic marriage between Abdallah Salum Muwinge and Halima Ismail. The Primary Court granted divorce, divided the matrimonial property and ordered child maintenance. Abdallah challenged the award of 70% of the matrimonial property to Halima and the monthly maintenance order of TZS 50,000. Before deciding those grounds, the High Court discovered that significant pages containing the petitioner’s testimony were missing from the Primary Court record. Because the appellate record was incomplete, the High Court nullified the proceedings and judgments of both lower courts and ordered a fresh trial before another magistrate with new assessors. No costs were awarded.',
      
