      relevantPassage: 'The High Court found that the alleged share transfer was not proved. It accepted the evidence showing that Marthinsen and Holte were outside Tanzania on the alleged signing date and found the transfer documents not genuine. Ulf Nilsson’s possession of the title was therefore lawful, and the plaintiff’s suit was dismissed.',
      fullTextSummary: 'Golden Reef Ltd sued Ulf Nilsson, claiming that he wrongfully possessed Certificate of Title No. 45952 for Plot No. 15, Block “A”, Kimbiji. The plaintiff sought return of the certificate, damages, interest and costs. The dispute depended on who lawfully controlled Golden Reef Ltd. Captain Lazarus Abel Sanga and Meinrad Florian Haule claimed that Lloyd Marthinsen and Otto Arne Holte had transferred the company’s shares to them in 2008. Marthinsen and Holte denied transferring their shares and alleged that the transfer documents were forged, maintaining that they had entrusted the title deed to Ulf Nilsson for safekeeping before leaving Tanzania. The High Court held that the alleged share transfer was not genuine (passport stamps established Marthinsen and Holte were abroad on the signing date), that personal familiarity with signatures was insufficient without expert handwriting evidence, and that Nilsson held the certificate lawfully as an authorized custodian. The plaintiff’s suit was dismissed with costs against Sanga and Haule.',

