        evidenceExamined: 'Trial record of Criminal Case No. 445 of 2019, handwritten vs typed minutes, testimony of victim (PW1), bystander witnesses (PW2, PW3), police witness (PW4), and expunged PF3 medical report.',
        legalTestsApplied: 'Section 214 continuation test; Section 226 trial in absentia test; Section 388 curability test; medical document tendering rule; daylight identification of known suspect doctrine.',
        lowerCourtProblems: 'Trial court improperly admitted PF3 through non-author police witness and omitted statutory sections in judgment conclusion.',
        whyArgumentsAcceptedRejected: 'Appellant’s objection to PF3 accepted and document expunged; all other grounds rejected because visual identification was foolproof, trial in absentia was justified, and judgment defects were harmless.',
        conclusionPathway: 'PF3 expunged; convictions for unnatural offence and assault ABH affirmed on credible direct and corroborative evidence; sentences upheld.'
