      ratioDecidendi: {
        coreRatio: 'A party seeking revision of a CMA award must strictly comply with the mandatory requirement of Regulation 34(1) of G.N. No. 47 of 2017 by lodging CMA Form No. 10 (Notice of Intention to Seek Revision) at the CMA. Where no genuine explanation is offered for the default, the overriding objective cannot cure the omission, and the revision is incurably incompetent and must be struck out.',
        legalTest: 'Mandatory Notice of Revision Test: (1) Check whether CMA Form No. 10 was lodged at the CMA; (2) Assess whether any plausible explanation is given for the omission; (3) If unexplained, the failure is a breach of a mandatory statutory prerequisite that cannot be bypassed via the overriding objective.',
        practicalApplication: 'An employer or employee filing a labour revision in the High Court must lodge CMA Form No. 10 with the CMA before or when instituting the application; failure to do so subjects the revision to being struck out on preliminary objection.'
      },

