      // 10. Ratio Decidendi
      ratioDecidendi: {
        coreRatio: 'Visual recognition by a prior acquaintance under favourable lighting over several hours is watertight evidence of identity, even where formal identification parades are invalidated by non-compliance with PGO No. 232. Retracted cautioned statements corroborated by eyewitness testimony are admissible, and an alibi shown to be fabricated by official registry records corroborates prosecution evidence. Under Section 23 of the Penal Code, all participants in an armed robbery are guilty of murder where lethal force was used with malice aforethought.',
        legalTest: 'Murder during Joint Robbery Test: (1) Water-tightness of visual recognition; (2) Evaluation of PGO 232 compliance; (3) Voluntariness and independent corroboration of confessions; (4) Objective disproof of alibi; (5) Common intention under Section 23; (6) Inference of malice aforethought under Section 200.',
        practicalApplication: 'In armed robbery-homicides, flawed police parade registers do not defeat convictions if surviving victims reliably recognized an attacker, co-accused gave voluntary corroborated statements, and documentary evidence exposes the accused’s alibi as a falsehood.'
      },

