        reasoning: 'The High Court held that the purported visual identification of Edward Maganga by neighbour Abel William was unreliable and improbable—it was unrealistic that armed nighttime killers would remain exposed to a torch for 15 minutes at a distance of seven metres or that a terrified witness would continuously illuminate them. Furthermore, all accused retracted their cautioned and extra-judicial statements, alleging police torture and showing that they had previously denied the offence before a magistrate before being taken to a Ward Executive Officer. The Court ruled that disputed co-accused confessions cannot corroborate one another because corroboration must originate from independent sources.',
        finalDecision: 'All three accused persons (Majuto Ngamba alias Ntumbi, Edward Maganga alias Tungu, and Paschal January alias Malosha) were found not guilty and acquitted of murder. The Court ordered their immediate release from custody unless lawfully held on other legal grounds.',
