        background: 'The land dispute originated in Kaselya Ward Tribunal (Land Case No. 07 of 2018) and proceeded on appeal to the District Land and Housing Tribunal for Iramba at Kiomboi (Land Appeal Case No. 08 of 2019), which ruled in favour of Jumanne Omary. Shaban Juma Kisonga sought extension of time to appeal to the High Court, which was granted on 28 March 2022 in Misc. Land Application No. 38 of 2020 (60 days to file appeal). Shaban lodged Miscellaneous Land Appeal No. 23 of 2022 on 27 May 2022. Jumanne raised two preliminary objections alleging the appeal was time-barred and fatally incompetent due to an undated Memorandum of Appeal.',
