      executiveSummary: 'The High Court dismissed Richard Amnaay\'s land appeal, affirming the District Land and Housing Tribunal\'s decision that approximately three acres of land at Endashangwet Village belonged to Phillipo Daffi Lolo. The Court held that the party asserting ownership bears the burden of proving it on a balance of probabilities under Sections 110 and 111 of the Evidence Act. Amnaay\'s unsupported oral assertion of village allocation during Operesheni Vijiji in 1975 was outweighed by Lolo\'s unchallenged documentary exhibits (Exhibit D1 sale agreement of 1973 for three goats from Baha Hondi and Exhibit D2 gift document of 1981 from his mother). Furthermore, Amnaay failed to object to or cross-examine Lolo on the documents at trial, and his subsequent allegation of forgery failed because allegations of fraud in civil cases require strict proof to a heightened standard of probability.',
