      ratioDecidendi: 'Official communications concerning a university or church administrative decision are not defamatory merely because they negatively affect the person concerned. Where an authorized official has a legal, moral, or social duty to communicate information to persons with a corresponding legitimate interest in receiving it, the communication is protected by qualified privilege unless the claimant proves express malice. Furthermore, a claimant must base their case strictly on pleaded facts, and employment disputes previously determined by the Industrial Court cannot be reopened indirectly through an unamended defamation claim.',
