      executiveSummary: 'The High Court dismissed the land appeal brought by seller Safari Arra and subsequent buyer Mogusha Joseph, affirming the District Land and Housing Tribunal\'s judgment declaring Paulo Yakobo the lawful owner of the disputed land. The Court held that despite differences in stated acreage (9 acres vs 6 acres) and village descriptions (Magara Village vs Maweni Village), both 2008 and 2009 sale agreements described precisely the same neighbouring boundaries (Jerome Ngalawa on East, Juma Ramadhani on West, Magdalena on South). Applying the priority principle (Ombeni Kimaro v Joseph Mishili), Paulo\'s purchase in 2008 was first in time; having completely divested himself of title, Safari possessed no remaining legal interest to convey to Mogusha in 2009. Safari Arra was ordered to pay the costs of both courts, and the DLHT order directing Safari to compensate Mogusha remained in force.',
