      fileName: 'Alfa Ramadhani Athuman v Republic 2024 TZHC 11161 (31 December 2024).pdf',
      summary: 'Alfa Ramadhani Athuman was convicted by the Resident Magistrates’ Court at Singida of raping an 18-year-old woman at Chungu Village, Ikungi District, and sentenced to 30 years’ imprisonment. On appeal, the High Court (F.D. Musokwa, J.) treated the matter as an adult complainant case requiring proof of penetration and absence of consent. The Court found material credibility doubts in the complainant’s claim that she remained with the appellant for ~3 hours (6:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m.) and accompanied him to her residence. Furthermore, a 2-hour discrepancy regarding the mother’s arrival time (11:00 p.m. vs. 1:00 a.m.) was held to be material rather than minor. Crucially, the prosecution failed to call the landlord who received the first disclosure and lent his phone to call the mother, justifying an adverse inference under Samweli Japhet Kahay v Republic. The High Court allowed the appeal in its entirety, quashed the conviction, set aside the 30-year sentence, and ordered Alfa’s immediate release.',
