      summary: 'Bank of Africa Tanzania Limited applied to the Court of Appeal for a stay of execution of the High Court (Labour Division) decision in Labour Revision No. 53 of 2022 (Dyasobera, J.), which upheld a CMA award in favour of former employees Patrick Mashele (Relationship Manager) and Felix Jia (Branch Manager). The CMA had declared their termination unfair and ordered reinstatement without loss of remuneration, or alternatively 12 months’ compensation plus terminal benefits. In Labour Execution Application No. 29 of 2023, the employees sought execution of TZS 686,374,785 via property attachment. The Court of Appeal (F.L.K. Wambali, J.A.) held that execution of such a colossal sum posed a serious risk of substantial loss if the intended appeal succeeded, given the respondents’ unknown financial capacity for restitution. The Court further ruled that a firm undertaking to provide security suffices under Rule 11(5)(b) of the Court of Appeal Rules without requiring pre-deposit. The Court granted a conditional stay ordering the bank to deposit a bank guarantee of TZS 686,374,785 within 45 days, with costs abiding the intended appeal.',
