      summary: 'Charles Mbwana applied under Section 14(1) of the Law of Limitation Act for extension of time to file an appeal against a matrimonial judgment of the District Court of Temeke (Hon. A.H. Mbadjo, SRM in Matrimonial Cause No. 66 of 2009 delivered 26 October 2023). The applicant claimed he was prevented from appealing within the 45-day statutory deadline (which expired on 10 December 2023) because the newly introduced electronic case management system (eCMS) required a case reference number that was unavailable. His advocate wrote to the in-charge magistrate on 8 November 2023 and claimed the number was supplied only on 1 August 2024. He also contended that the intended appeal involved apparent illegalities concerning property division at Mlandizi, contribution evaluation, adultery, and DNA testing for child paternity. The High Court (S.D. Mwaipopo, J.) dismissed the application, holding that the applicant failed to prove continuous diligence under the Lyamuya Construction rules, as no written reminders or proof of physical follow-ups between November 2023 and August 2024 were produced. Furthermore, alleged misappreciation of evidence does not constitute an apparent illegality on the face of the record. Costs were ordered to be shared by the parties.',
