      ratioDecidendi: 'A matrimonial proceeding does not necessarily abate when one spouse dies after the hearing has been concluded but before judgment is delivered. Where matrimonial legislation does not prescribe the procedure, Order XXII Rule 6 of the Civil Procedure Code applies to fill the procedural gap. The court may pronounce judgment based on the completed hearing, and that judgment has the same force and effect as if delivered before the party’s death.',
