      fileName: 'Majanja Lukamba Vs Charles Zacharia and 2 others 2024 TZHC 11081 (27 December 2024).pdf',
      summary: 'Majanja Lukamba applied to the High Court under Section 11(1) of the Appellate Jurisdiction Act for an extension of time to file a notice of appeal and an appeal against a High Court land judgment delivered on 13 October 2023 in Land Appeal No. 43 of 2023 (originating from Muleba DLHT Land Application No. 33 of 2021). The applicant filed his application on 9 May 2024, approximately six months after the judgment, relying on illness and alleged illegality in the decision. The High Court (G.P. Malata, J.) dismissed the application with costs, holding that medical check-up sheets for six isolated dates (8 Oct 2023, 5 Nov 2023, 19 Dec 2023, 8 Mar 2024, 21 Mar 2024, 16 Apr 2024) failed to explain over 170 days of continuous delay or establish that the applicant was continuously incapacitated. Furthermore, the alleged illegality was not apparent on the face of the record or capable of excusing prolonged inactivity, and neither the applicant nor his retained advocate took diligent steps to initiate the appeal.',
