        respondentArguments: 'Mr. Tumaini Mfinanga argued that: (1) The applicant failed to satisfy the Atilio v. Mbowe tri-partite test; (2) A marriage certificate alone does not prove that property owned by a corporate borrower is matrimonial property; (3) Tanzanian law recognizes separate property of spouses; (4) The applicant failed to tender documentary title evidence establishing ownership (citing Trustees of Anglican Church Diocese of Western Tanganyika v. Bulimanyi Village Council); (5) Irreparable loss was not proven by concrete quantifiable evidence; (6) An injunction cannot be used to prevent a bona fide purchaser from enjoying property purchased after a loan default; (7) Application should be dismissed with costs.'
