      ratioDecidendi: 'A grant of letters of administration will not be revoked for fraud or concealment under Section 49 of the Probate and Administration of Estates Act unless the applicant produces cogent and compelling evidence demonstrating that the administrators knowingly made a false material statement or intentionally withheld material facts. Open disclosure of a person treated as a family member, combined with the applicant’s attendance, execution of Form No. 56 consent, and failure to lodge a caveat, creates an estoppel and defeats an allegation of fraudulent concealment. Furthermore, the appointment of administrators is legally distinct from the final determination of heirship and beneficial entitlement, which may be determined at subsequent stages of estate administration.',
