      ratioDecidendi: 'An action or appeal instituted in the name of a person who was already dead at the time of filing is a nullity and incurably incompetent. A deceased person lacks legal personality and capacity to give instructions to an advocate. The appearance of an advocate cannot cure the fatal defect, and a duly appointed administrator or personal representative must be formally joined or substituted before proceedings can validly be instituted or prosecuted.',
