        'REBUTTABLE PRESUMPTION FOR MATERNAL CUSTODY: For a child of tender years below seven, Section 26(2) and Section 39 establish a rebuttable presumption in favour of the mother. A father’s capability and financial stability do not displace this presumption without convincing proof of maternal unfitness, incapacity, or demonstrable harm.',
