      ratioDecidendi: 'For a child of tender years below seven, Section 26(2) and Section 39 of the Law of the Child Act create a statutory rebuttable presumption that custody with the mother serves the child’s best interests. This presumption cannot be displaced merely because the father is also capable, financially stable, or willing to provide care; it requires clear and convincing evidence of maternal unfitness, neglect, or demonstrable harm. Furthermore, while a social inquiry report assists the court under Rule 72 of the Juvenile Court Procedure Rules, the court must independently evaluate its balance, factual foundation, and admissibility, and cannot substitute the social welfare officer’s opinion for judicial decision-making.',
