      ratioDecidendi: 'A plea of guilty is unequivocal under Section 245 of the Criminal Procedure Act where the charge is read and explained, the accused clearly admits the charge, the prosecution narrates facts disclosing every constituent element of the offence, and the accused unequivocally admits those facts without qualification. A detailed admission describing forceful non-consensual sexual penetration proves full understanding of the offence. Following a valid guilty plea, the omission to read aloud supporting documents (such as PF3 or caution statements) placed on the record does not prejudice the accused or vitiate the conviction. Under Section 360(1) of the CPA, an appeal against conviction is barred once an unequivocal plea of guilty is established.',
