      ratioDecidendi: 'The High Court’s criminal revisional jurisdiction under Section 372(1) of the Criminal Procedure Act is not confined to final judgments or sentences; it extends to examining the regularity of ongoing trial proceedings in subordinate courts where fundamental procedural defects undermine trial fairness. In recording cross-examination, a trial magistrate must transcribe the evidence in such a manner—either by recording both question and answer or by using a coherent narrative form—that the context, substance, and meaning of the witness’s responses are fully intelligible. Transcribing isolated, disconnected answers without questions creates a fatal defect that deprives the court and appellate tribunals of a reliable record, justifying the nullification and fresh retaking of the cross-examination.',
