      fileType: 'PDF',
      rawExtractedText: `IN THE HIGH COURT OF TANZANIA, DODOMA DISTRICT REGISTRY
MISCELLANEOUS LAND APPEAL NO. 23 OF 2022
(Arising from Land Appeal Case No. 08 of 2019 of the District Land and Housing Tribunal for Iramba at Kiomboi / Land Case No. 07 of 2018 Kaselya Ward Tribunal)

SHABAN JUMA KISONGA (As Legal Representative of the Estate of the Late Pili Selemani Kiula) ... APPELLANT
VERSUS
JUMANNE OMARY (As Legal Representative of the Estate of the Late Omary Mjange Dudu) ........... RESPONDENT

RULING
GEORGE M. MASAJU, J. (Delivered on 27 December 2022):

1. CASE SUMMARY:
Shaban Juma Kisonga (representing the estate of the late Pili Selemani Kiula) appealed against the land decision of the Iramba District Land and Housing Tribunal in Land Appeal Case No. 08 of 2019 in favour of Jumanne Omary (representing the estate of the late Omary Mjange Dudu). The respondent raised preliminary objections that the appeal was time-barred beyond the 60-day period granted in Misc. Land Application No. 38 of 2020 on 28 March 2022, and that the Memorandum of Appeal was fatally incompetent for want of a date. The High Court overruled both objections: (1) 60 days counted from 28 March 2022 expired on 27 May 2022, the precise date of filing, and Section 19 of the Law of Limitation Act excludes time to obtain proceedings; (2) The Memorandum was signed and officially stamped by the registry on 27 May 2022, curing the technical omission of a handwritten date. The appellant was permitted to insert the date 27 May 2022, and the substantive appeal remained competent.

2. MATERIAL FACTS:
- Originating land dispute in Kaselya Ward Tribunal (Land Case No. 07 of 2018).
- Appellated to Iramba DLHT at Kiomboi (Land Appeal Case No. 08 of 2019) in favour of Jumanne Omary.
- High Court granted Shaban 60 days to file appeal on 28 March 2022 in Misc. Land Application No. 38 of 2020.
- Appeal lodged in registry on 27 May 2022 with signature but no handwritten date.
- Registry officially endorsed and stamped filing on 27 May 2022.

3. LEGAL ISSUES:
- Was the appeal filed outside the 60-day extension period? (No; filed on 60th day).
- Does Section 19 Law of Limitation Act apply? (Yes; time to obtain copies is excluded).
- Does an undated Memorandum of Appeal render the appeal incurably incompetent? (No; official registry filing stamp cures defect).

4. LAWS CITED:
- Law of Limitation Act, Cap. 89 R.E. 2019 (Section 19)

5. FINAL DECISION AND ORDERS:
1. Preliminary objection on limitation: OVERRULED.
2. Preliminary objection on undated Memorandum: OVERRULED.
3. Miscellaneous Land Appeal No. 23 of 2022 declared competent.
4. Appellant permitted to insert date 27 May 2022 on Memorandum of Appeal.
5. Each party to bear own costs.`,
