      rawExtractedText: `IN THE HIGH COURT OF TANZANIA, DAR ES SALAAM DISTRICT REGISTRY
MISCELLANEOUS CIVIL APPLICATION NO. 560 OF 2022 / [2022] TZHC 15474
(Arising from Civil Case No. 147 of 2020)

VIGU TRADING COMPANY LIMITED ............................................ APPLICANT
VERSUS
1. BANK OF AFRICA TANZANIA LIMITED
2. NAMPULA AUCTION MART AND COMPANY LIMITED
3. BILO STAR DEBT COLLECTOR CO. LTD ..................................... RESPONDENTS

RULING
H. R. MWANGA, J. (Delivered on 23 December 2022):

1. CASE SUMMARY:
Vigu Trading Company Limited obtained credit facilities of ~USD 2.8 million from Bank of Africa Tanzania Limited secured by ~100 trucks and trailers. While Civil Case No. 147 of 2020 was undergoing court mediation over debt balances and recovery fees exceeding TZS 140 million, the bank engaged Nampula Auction Mart (who seized 27 vehicles in 2020) and Bilo Star Debt Collector (targeting 18 more vehicles in 2022) to impound and auction the fleet. Vigu applied in Misc. Civil Application No. 560 of 2022 for an interim status quo order. The High Court granted the order, holding that the application was directly connected to the pending suit, that non-joinder of the debt collector in the 2020 suit did not sever jurisdiction, that preservation was vital during active mediation, and that the bank demonstrated no injustice.

2. MATERIAL FACTS:
- 2013-2016: Banking facilities of ~USD 2.8 million advanced to Vigu Trading secured by ~100 trucks and trailers.
- Outstanding dispute over remaining balance (~USD 600,000, with USD 299,793.59 paid) and recovery costs (>TZS 140 million).
- Civil Case No. 147 of 2020 pending and referred to court-supervised mediation.
- 27 vehicles seized in Oct 2020; 18 additional vehicles targeted by Bilo Star in late 2022.
- Misc. Civil Application No. 560 of 2022 filed seeking interim preservation of status quo.

3. LEGAL ISSUES:
- Should the court preserve the status quo pending determination of the application? (Yes).
- Is the application sufficiently connected to Civil Case No. 147 of 2020? (Yes).
- Did the addition of Bilo Star Debt Collector sever the nexus with the main suit? (No).
- Did respondents demonstrate injustice? (No).

4. LAWS CITED:
- Inherent jurisdiction and general principles of civil procedure and equity regarding interim preservation of property and maintenance of status quo.

5. FINAL DECISION AND ORDERS:
1. Application for interim status quo order GRANTED.
2. Respondents and agents RESTRAINED from impounding, seizing, or selling trucks and trailers in Schedule TAB-1.
3. Restraint remains in force pending determination of application on the merits.`,
