      category: 'Criminal Law, Rape, Identification vs Penetration, and Witness Credibility',
      description: 'High Court criminal appeal allowing appeal, quashing two concurrent 30-year rape convictions, and ordering immediate release; holding that medical proof of penetration and child age does not prove perpetrator identity where material contradictions surround disclosure and discovery, medical evidence fails to corroborate alleged foul smell, and chain of evidence is incomplete under Section 143 of Evidence Act.',
      accessLevel: 'Public Legal Library',
