      downloadUrl: 'https://tanzlii.org/tz/judgment/high-court-tanzania/2024/11152/download/pdf',
      extractedText: 'IN THE HIGH COURT OF TANZANIA AT TEMEKE SUB-REGISTRY ONE STOP JUDICIAL CENTRE AT TEMEKE. CIVIL APPEAL NO. 28242 OF 2024 (Arising from PC Matrimonial Appeal No. 10532 of 2024 of the District Court of Temeke at Temeke, which originated in Matrimonial Cause No. 1855 of 2023 of the Primary Court of Temeke). CATHERINE EDWIN MBELE VERSUS GODFREY ABEDNEGO MUSHI. RULING. S.D. MWAIPOPO, J.: The appellant Catherine Edwin Mbele sought to appeal against a matrimonial decision that originated in Temeke Primary Court and was decided on first appeal by Temeke District Court. She filed a "Petition of Appeal" instead of a "Memorandum of Appeal" required under Rule 37(1) of the Law of Marriage (Matrimonial Proceedings) Rules [GN No. 246 of 1997], and registered the appeal as an ordinary "Civil Appeal" (Civil Appeal No. 28242 of 2024) instead of a "PC Civil Appeal". The respondent raised a preliminary objection on the use of a petition, and the Court on its own motion raised the improper registration. Mr. John Msifuni Msuya for the appellant invoked Article 107A(2)(e) of the Constitution and overriding objective principles, claiming the electronic system rejected PC categories. Mr. Nehemia Gabo for the respondent argued the defects were fatal. HELD: While interchanging petition and memorandum can be curable (Yakobo Magoiga Gichere v Peninnah Yusuph, Mary Mwambene v Benson Mwashambwa), registering a Primary Court-originating appeal in the ordinary Civil Appeal register violates Chief Justice’s Circular No. 2 of 2021. Such misregistration goes to the root of electronic case management and statistical classification (ASG Société Générale de Surveillance SA v VIP Engineering & Marketing Ltd). The appellant failed to prove electronic filing malfunction under Section 110 Evidence Act. Appeal rejected and struck out with leave to refile in the proper PC Civil Appeal register with a memorandum of appeal within 21 days. No order as to costs. [Duplicate Scan Verification: Recorded under both [2024] TZHC 11152 and [2024] TZHC 11406 across 2 PDF files, confirmed identical in text, bench, reasoning, and orders, and merged into canonical record TZHC-2024-CIVIL-28242].',
